===Motivation===

[[bip-0327.mediawiki|BIP327]] (MuSig2) allows a flat set of ''n'' co-signers to
create a single aggregate public key and cooperatively produce an ordinary
Schnorr signature that verifies under [[bip-0340.mediawiki|BIP340]]. The
aggregate public key is computed from the individual public keys of all
participants, and the resulting signature is indistinguishable from a signature
created by a single signer holding the corresponding aggregate secret key.

MuSig2 is an ''n''-of-''n'' multi-signature scheme in which every signer whose
public key is included in the aggregate key must participate in each signing
session. After the aggregate key has been established, signers exchange public
nonces and then partial signatures, allowing signing to complete in two
communication rounds.

This model works well when the signing group is naturally flat: each participant
is a single logical signer, and every participant is expected to contribute to
every signature. However, many Bitcoin applications are not naturally flat. A
participant in one protocol may itself be a signing group with its own internal
MuSig2 aggregate key, coordination process, and availability assumptions.
Flattening all such internal keys into a single MuSig2 aggregate removes this
group structure and treats every leaf key as a direct participant in one global
signing session.

In such applications, flattening can have several undesirable effects. It can
reveal internal signer sets to other protocol participants, require parties
outside a group to reason about that group's internal key structure, and make
the outer protocol depend directly on every individual leaf signer rather than
on logical signer groups.

Consider the following examples:

* '''Institutional custody''': a custodian may operate several geographically separated signing devices under an internal MuSig2 policy. Externally, the custodian may appear as one logical signer in a protocol shared with a client or another institution. Flattening the custodian's internal keys together with the external participant's keys exposes the custodian's internal signer set to the counterparty and makes the external protocol depend directly on every internal device.

* '''Lightning channel factories''': a channel factory may involve participants that are themselves represented by MuSig2 signing groups. Flattening every underlying key into one aggregate key removes the distinction between participants and their internal signing groups. It also turns signing into a single all-leaf-signers-required protocol rather than a protocol between logical participants.

* '''Ark-style VTXO trees''': Ark and related constructions organize virtual UTXOs using trees of off-chain transactions. When aggregate keys are used at multiple levels of such a construction, a flat list of all leaf keys does not naturally preserve the hierarchical relationship between transaction-tree nodes and signing groups.

* '''Corporate treasury''': an executive group, a compliance group, and a finance group may each maintain separate MuSig2 signing arrangements. A final treasury authorization may require participation by each group while keeping each group's internal signer set hidden from the others. Flattening all keys into one aggregate exposes those internal structures and makes the protocol depend on every individual leaf signer.

NestedMuSig2 addresses this by allowing a participant public key at one level of
a MuSig2 signing session to itself be a MuSig2 aggregate key. The result is a
tree of signing groups whose root key is still an ordinary BIP340-compatible
x-only public key, and whose final signature is still an ordinary BIP340
signature.

This preserves the verifier-facing properties of MuSig2. A verifier only sees a
BIP340 public key and a BIP340 signature. The verifier does not need to know
whether the signing key was produced by a single signer, a flat MuSig2 group, or
a nested tree of MuSig2 groups.

NestedMuSig2 also preserves the two-round signing structure of MuSig2. Each leaf
signer participates in one nonce-exchange round and one partial-signature round,
while aggregation is performed recursively by coordinators at each level of the
tree.

This BIP specifies the additional nonce aggregation, signing, and partial
signature aggregation rules required to make such recursive composition
well-defined and compatible with BIP340 verification.

==Algorithms==

This BIP builds directly on BIP327. The notation and helper functions ''int(x)'', ''bytes(k, x)'', ''cbytes'', ''cbytes_ext'', ''xbytes'', ''cpoint'', ''cpoint_ext'', ''has_even_y'', the tagged-hash construction ''hash<sub>tag</sub>''), and primitive algorithms not explicitly redefined here are inherited from [[bip-0327.mediawiki|BIP327]]. In particular, the BIP327 algorithms ''IndividualPubkey'', ''KeySort'', ''KeyAgg'', ''KeyAggCoeff'', ''GetXonlyPubkey'', ''GetPlainPubkey'', ''ApplyTweak'', ''NonceGen'' and ''NonceAgg'' are used unchanged and are not restated in this specification.

This specification replaces the BIP327 Session Context and the algorithms ''GetSessionValues'', ''GetSessionKeyAggCoeff'', ''Sign'', ''PartialSigVerify'', ''PartialSigVerifyInternal'', and ''PartialSigAgg'' with the nested versions specified below. It also introduces the new algorithm ''NonceAggExt''. No other BIP327 algorithm is incorporated by implication.

This specification follows BIP327's distinction between ordinary failures and failures attributable to another party. ''Fail'' means that the algorithm terminates without producing an output. If the specification additionally instructs the implementation to blame a party for an invalid contribution, the failure is an ''InvalidContribution'' failure. Implementations SHOULD record the type of invalid contribution and the identity of the party to be blamed.

===Notation===

The following notation is used in addition to the notation of BIP327. A signing session is described from the perspective of a single leaf signer. The corresponding objects in the referenced paper <ref name="paper" /> are noted where the mapping is not obvious.

The group order ''p'' in the paper corresponds to the secp256k1 group order ''n'' in this specification. The BIP327 key-aggregation hashes instantiate the role of ''H<sub>agg</sub>'' using the optimized key-aggregation construction. The paper's intermediate nonce hash ''H<sub>non</sub>'', root nonce hash ''H&#773;<sub>non</sub>'', and signature hash ''H<sub>sig</sub>'' correspond to ''hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>'', ''hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>'', and ''hash<sub>BIP0340/challenge</sub>'', respectively.

* ''&Lambda;'' is the number of aggregation levels on the path from the signer to the root, with ''&Lambda; &ge; 1''. Levels are indexed''d = 0, ..., &Lambda;−1'' from the root toward the signer. Level ''0'' produces the root aggregate key, and level ''&Lambda;−1'' is the signer's own aggregation level. ''&Lambda; = 1'' is the flat BIP327 case. Different leaves in the same signing tree MAY have different values of ''&Lambda;''.

* The following objects are local to the leaf signer executing ''Sign''. They do not denote global values shared by every node at the same depth.

** ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' is the plain public key by which the signer is represented at level ''d''. At level ''&Lambda;−1'', it is the signer's individual public key. For ''d < &Lambda;−1'', it is the plain aggregate public key of the subtree containing the signer at level ''d+1''. It corresponds to ''pk<sub>1,d</sub>'' in the paper<ref name="paper" />.

** ''T<sub>d</sub>'' is the multiset of cosigner plain public keys at level ''d'', excluding the distinguished participant occurrence represented by ''pk<sub>d</sub>''. It contains one public key for every other participant at that aggregation node. Each element is either an individual public key or the aggregate plain public key of a nested subtree; the signer neither knows nor needs to know which. In the notation of the referenced paper<ref name="paper" />, ''T<sub>d</sub>'' corresponds to ''{pk<sub>i,d</sub>}<sub>2≤i≤n<sub>d</sub></sub>'', where the index starts at 2 because ''pk<sub>1,d</sub>'' denotes the signer's own key at level ''d'' and is therefore excluded from ''T<sub>d</sub>''. ''T<sub>d</sub>'' MAY contain a public key that is byte-for-byte identical to ''pk<sub>d</sub>'', because BIP327 permits duplicate public keys. ''T<sub>d</sub>'' MAY be empty.

** ''L<sub>d</sub>'' is the ordered key list ''L<sub>d</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>d</sub>} ∪ T<sub>d</sub>)''. For ''d > 0'', let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)'' and ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub>)''. Thus, ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' is the 33-byte plain public key by which the level-''d'' subtree participates at level ''d−1''. The output of ''GetPlainPubkey(KeyAgg(L<sub>0</sub>))'' is the untweaked root aggregate public key.

** ''a<sub>d</sub>'' is the BIP327 key-aggregation coefficient ''a<sub>d</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d</sub>)''. The scalar ''a<sub>0</sub>·...·a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n'' is the signer's recursive key-aggregation coefficient. Root tweaking and X-only parity adjustments are handled separately by the nested signing algorithm.

* ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is the 66-byte internal aggregate nonce at the level-''d'' aggregation node on the signer's path. It is the output of ''NonceAgg'' applied to the first-round nonce contributions of all participants at that node. For ''d > 0'', ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is not used directly as the subtree's contribution to the parent. Instead, the subtree contributes the external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt(out<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d−1</sub>)''. The sequence ''out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>'' is called the signer's nonce path.

* For ''d = 1, ..., &Lambda;−1'', ''b<sub>d</sub>'' is the intermediate nonce-binding factor derived from ''out<sub>d</sub>'' and the 33-byte plain public key ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>''. It is the same factor used by ''NonceAggExt'' to derive the subtree's external nonce. Intermediate binding factors do not commit to the message.

* ''b<sub>0</sub>'' is the BIP327 root nonce-binding factor derived from ''out<sub>0</sub>'', the X-only root aggregate public key used for signing, and the message. If root-level tweaks are applied, the aggregate public key after all tweaks is used. This is the only nonce-binding factor that commits to the message.

* ''b&#780;'' is the accumulated nonce-binding factor ''b&#780; = b<sub>0</sub>·...·b<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''. With two nonces, ''b&#780;'' multiplies the signer's second secret nonce in the nested partial-signature equation.

* ''c'' is the ordinary BIP340 challenge computed from the final nonce point, the X-only root public key used for signing, and the message.

* ''c&#780;'' is the accumulated challenge coefficient ''c&#780; = c·a<sub>0</sub>·...·a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''. It is the coefficient associated with the signer's secret key before applying the root KeyAgg Context's parity and tweak adjustments.

* Let ''out<sub>0</sub> = cbytes_ext(R<sub>1,0</sub>) || cbytes_ext(R<sub>2,0</sub>)''. First compute ''R' = R<sub>1,0</sub> + b<sub>0</sub>·R<sub>2,0</sub>''. If ''R''' is the point at infinity, let ''R = G''. Otherwise, let ''R = R''''. Intermediate nonce-binding factors do not appear explicitly in this expression because they have already been applied by ''NonceAggExt'' as nested nonce contributions flowed toward the root.

===Tagged Hashes===

Tagged hashes follow the BIP340 construction ''SHA256(SHA256(tag) || SHA256(tag) || x)'', where ''tag'' is a UTF-8 encoded string. 

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Tag string !! Used in
|-
| <code>KeyAgg list</code>, <code>KeyAgg coefficient</code> || ''KeyAgg'' and ''KeyAggCoeff'', unchanged from BIP327 and invoked independently at each aggregation level
|-
| <code>MuSig/aux</code> || Auxiliary-randomness derivation in ''NonceGen'', unchanged from BIP327
|-
| <code>MuSig/nonce</code> || Secret-nonce derivation in ''NonceGen'', unchanged from BIP327
|- 
| <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code> || ''NonceAggExt'' and the intermediate nonce binding factors ''b<sub>1</sub>, ..., b<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>''
|-
| <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> || Root binding factor ''b<sub>0</sub>'', unchanged from BIP327
|-
| <code>BIP0340/challenge</code> || The Schnorr signature challenge, unchanged from BIP340
|}

The tags <code>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</code> and <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> serve distinct random-oracle roles and MUST remain distinct. Retaining <code>MuSig/noncecoef</code> at the root ensures that the protocol reduces exactly to BIP327 when ''&Lambda; = 1'' and allows a nested subtree to participate as one signer in an otherwise unmodified BIP327 signing session.

The key-aggregation tags are unchanged from BIP327. Consequently, every aggregation node produces the same aggregate key that BIP327 produces for the same ordered plain-public-key list.

The challenge tag is unchanged from BIP340. Consequently, the final signature is a standard BIP340 signature and can be verified using an unmodified BIP340 verifier.

===Key Generation and Aggregation===

This specification uses the BIP327 algorithms ''IndividualPubkey'', ''KeySort'', ''KeyAgg'', ''KeyAggCoeff'', ''GetPlainPubkey'', ''GetXonlyPubkey'', and ''ApplyTweak'' unchanged. All input requirements, failure conditions, and serialization rules defined by those algorithms apply.

====Nested Key Aggregation====
Key aggregation is performed independently at every aggregation node. For a node at level ''d'' on a particular signer's path, let ''L<sub>d</sub>'' be the ''KeySort''-sorted list of participant plain public keys belonging to that node. The node's KeyAgg Context is computed as:''keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)''.

Each aggregation node MUST create its own fresh KeyAgg Context using only the participant plain public keys belonging to that node. A child node's KeyAgg Context MUST NOT be used as an input to the parent node's KeyAgg invocation. For every non-root node at level ''d'', the node's aggregate public key is obtained using ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub>)''. The resulting 33-byte plain public key ''pk<sub>d−1</sub>'' is used as a participant plain public key in the parent node's participant key list at level ''d-1''. Only the serialized plain public key is propagated between aggregation levels. The complete child KeyAgg Context is local to the child aggregation node and MUST NOT be propagated upward.

In particular, the ''gacc'' and ''tacc'' values of an intermediate KeyAgg Context MUST NOT be propagated across aggregation levels. Each aggregation node MUST derive its aggregation state from the fresh KeyAgg Context returned by ''KeyAgg'' for its own participant key list.

====Intermediate Aggregate Key Representation====
Using ''GetPlainPubkey'' preserves the parity of the intermediate aggregate point. Intermediate aggregate keys MUST therefore be represented as 33-byte BIP327 plain public keys and MUST NOT be converted to x-only public keys before being used as participant keys in a parent node's ''KeyAgg'' invocation. The parity information contained in the plain public key serialization is required because the intermediate aggregate key is interpreted as a participant plain public key at the next aggregation level.

Intermediate aggregate public keys do not require explicit protocol transmission. Any participant that knows the complete nested public-key tree MUST be able to independently compute every intermediate aggregate public key.

====Root Aggregation====
The root node is aggregated using the same procedure as all other aggregation nodes. The root KeyAgg Context is computed as ''keyagg_ctx_root = KeyAgg(L<sub>0</sub>)'' where ''L<sub>0</sub>'' is the ''KeySort''-sorted list of participant plain public keys at the root level.

====Root-Level Aggregate-Key Tweaking====
If the application specifies root-level aggregate-key tweaks, they MUST be applied sequentially to ''keyagg_ctx_root'' using ''ApplyTweak''. All participants MUST apply the same ordered sequence of tweaks. For each tweak, participants MUST use the corresponding ''is_xonly_t'' value specified by the application. After all root-level tweaks have been applied, ''keyagg_ctx_root'' refers to the final tweaked root KeyAgg Context. The final aggregate public key is obtained as ''aggpk = GetXonlyPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>0</sub>)''. 

The resulting 32-byte x-only public key ''aggpk'' is the public key used for BIP340 verification. The final tweaked root KeyAgg Context MUST be used by the nested signing algorithm, partial-signature verification algorithm, and final signature aggregation algorithm.

Root-level tweaks affect only the root KeyAgg Context. They MUST NOT be applied to intermediate aggregation nodes.

====Aggregate-Key Tweaking Restrictions====
Aggregate-key tweaking is supported only at the root level of the nested aggregation tree. ''ApplyTweak'' MUST NOT be applied to the KeyAgg Context of any non-root aggregation node. Tweaking an intermediate aggregate key would modify the relationship between intermediate aggregate keys and the nested signing equations. Supporting such tweaks would require corresponding changes to the nested signing and partial-signature verification algorithms, which are not defined by this specification.

This restriction applies only to aggregate-key tweaking within the nested aggregation tree. It does not restrict how an individual participant derives its own secret key and corresponding plain public key before entering the protocol.

===Nonce Generation===

Each leaf signer generates its secret and public nonce using the BIP327 algorithm ''NonceGen'' unchanged. All input requirements, optional-argument encodings, failure conditions, tagged hashes, and output serialization rules of BIP327 ''NonceGen'' apply. In particular, ''NonceGen'' uses the tagged hashes <code>MuSig/aux</code> and <code>MuSig/nonce</code>. This specification does not introduce separate NestedMuSig2 tags for nonce generation. Implementations MUST NOT replace these tags with <code>NestedMuSig/aux</code>, <code>NestedMuSig/nonce</code>, or any other tags.

For a leaf signer whose path contains ''&Lambda;'' aggregation levels, the arguments supplied to ''NonceGen'' MUST satisfy:
* The mandatory ''pk'' argument MUST be the signer's 33-byte individual plain public key ''pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>''. It MUST NOT be an intermediate subgroup aggregate key or the root aggregate key.
* The optional ''sk'' argument, when provided, MUST be the secret signing key corresponding to ''pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>''. It SHOULD be provided whenever it is available to the nonce-generation component.
* The optional ''aggpk'' argument, when provided, MUST be the 32-byte x-only root aggregate public key after all key aggregation and all root-level tweaks have been applied. Equivalently, it is ''GetXonlyPubkey'' of the final root ''KeyAgg Context''. An intermediate subgroup aggregate key MUST NOT be supplied as ''aggpk''. If the final root aggregate public key is not known when nonces are generated, ''aggpk'' MAY be omitted.
* The optional message ''m'' SHOULD be provided if it is already known. It MAY be omitted when nonce generation is performed before the message is determined. As in BIP327, an omitted message is distinct from a present message of length zero.
* The optional ''extra_in'' argument MAY contain application-specific contextual data, as described in BIP327.

The serialized representation of ''secnonce'' is the 97-byte array ''bytes(32, k<sub>1</sub>) || bytes(32, k<sub>2</sub>) || pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>'', and the serialized representation of ''pubnonce'' is the 66-byte array ''cbytes(k<sub>1</sub>⋅G) || cbytes(k<sub>2</sub>⋅G)''. The ''secnonce'' is a local secret state and MUST NOT be transmitted to another participant. Implementations MAY represent it internally using a different data structure or an opaque handle, provided that the values ''k<sub>1</sub>'', ''k<sub>2</sub>'', and ''pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>'' are preserved with the same semantics. The 66-byte ''pubnonce'' is the leaf signer's first-round contribution to its immediate parent aggregation node.

''NonceGen'' MUST obtain its internal 32-byte value <code>rand'</code> from a cryptographically secure random number generator. It MUST be generated independently for each invocation using a cryptographically secure random number generator and MUST NOT be reused across invocations. The nonce scalars MUST NOT be derived deterministically from only the message, public keys, signing tree, or other adversary-influenced session parameters.

A ''secnonce'' MUST be supplied to at most one invocation of ''Sign'', including an invocation that subsequently fails. It MUST NOT be reused in another NestedMuSig2 session, a BIP327 session, or any other signing protocol. Implementations SHOULD enforce this requirement by keeping secret nonces behind opaque, single-use handles, atomically marking a handle as consumed before signing, and securely erasing the nonce scalars after consumption.

Only leaf signers invoke ''NonceGen''. An aggregation node representing a nested subgroup derives the subgroup's first-round contribution by applying ''NonceAgg'' and ''NonceAggExt'' to its participants' contributions; it MUST NOT invoke ''NonceGen'' to create a replacement nonce for the subgroup. 

===Nonce Aggregation===

The BIP327 algorithm ''NonceAgg'' is used unchanged at every aggregation node. All input requirements, failure conditions, serialization rules, and contributor-blame requirements of BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' apply.

During the first round, nonce aggregation proceeds from the leaves toward the root. A participant at an aggregation node contributes one of the following:
* A direct leaf signer contributes the 66-byte ''pubnonce'' returned by ''NonceGen''.
* A nested child aggregation node contributes the 66-byte external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt''.

For an aggregation node at level ''d'', nonce aggregation is performed as follows:
# The aggregator collects exactly one 66-byte first-round contribution for every participant occurrence in ''L<sub>d</sub>''. The number of contributions MUST equal the number of participant public keys in ''L<sub>d</sub>''.
# The aggregator computes ''out<sub>d</sub> = NonceAgg(contribution<sub>1</sub>, ..., contribution<sub>u</sub>)''.
#:The result ''out<sub>d</sub>'' is the node's '''internal aggregate nonce'''.
# If ''d > 0'', let ''keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub> = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)'' and ''pk<sub>d−1</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx<sub>d</sub>)''. The aggregator computes ''extnonce<sub>d</sub> = NonceAggExt(out<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d−1</sub>)'' and supplies ''extnonce<sub>d</sub>'' as the node's first-round contribution at level ''d−1''.
# If ''d = 0'', ''out<sub>0</sub>'' is the root internal aggregate nonce. It MUST NOT be passed through ''NonceAggExt''. 

At the root, the nonce binding factor is computed using the BIP327 tag and encoding ''b<sub>0</sub> = int(hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>(out<sub>0</sub> || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n'', where ''Q'' is the root aggregate public key after all root-level tweaks have been applied. This root computation is unchanged from BIP327.

When ''&Lambda; = 1'', no invocation of ''NonceAggExt'' occurs, and nonce aggregation reduces exactly to BIP327 nonce aggregation.

====Distribution of Internal Aggregate Nonces====

Each aggregation node MUST retain its internal aggregate nonce ''out<sub>d</sub>'' until the signing session has completed or aborted.
Before the second round, internal aggregate nonces are distributed from the root toward the leaves as follows:

# The root aggregator begins with the nonce-path prefix ''(out<sub>0</sub>)''.
# A non-root aggregator at level ''d'' receives the prefix ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>d−1</sub>)'' from its parent.
# It appends its stored internal aggregate nonce ''out<sub>d</sub>'' and forwards the resulting prefix ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>d</sub>)'' to each of its participants.
# A leaf signer whose path contains ''&Lambda;'' aggregation levels therefore receives ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)''.

Every value in the nonce path supplied to ''Sign'' MUST be an internal aggregate nonce returned by ''NonceAgg''. An external nonce returned by ''NonceAggExt'' MUST NOT be substituted for an internal aggregate nonce in this path.

Each non-root aggregation node MUST forward the same ''out<sub>d</sub>'' from which it derived the external nonce supplied to its parent.

====External Nonce Aggregation====
Algorithm ''NonceAggExt(aggnonce, pk_agg)'':
* Inputs:
** ''aggnonce'': the 66-byte internal aggregate nonce returned by ''NonceAgg'' for this aggregation node.
** ''pk_agg'': the 33-byte plain aggregate public key by which this aggregation node is represented at its parent node.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(aggnonce) &ne; 66''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(pk_agg) &ne; 33''.
* Let ''Q = cpoint(pk_agg)''; ''Fail'' if that fails.
* Let ''R'<sub>1</sub> = cpoint_ext(aggnonce[0:33])''; ''Fail'' if that fails.
* Let ''R'<sub>2</sub> = cpoint_ext(aggnonce[33:66])''; ''Fail'' if that fails.
* Let ''b = int(hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>(aggnonce || cbytes(Q))) mod n''.
* Let ''R<sub>1</sub> = R'<sub>1</sub>''.
* Let ''R<sub>2</sub> = b⋅R'<sub>2</sub>''.
* Return ''cbytes_ext(R<sub>1</sub>) || cbytes_ext(R<sub>2</sub>)''.

The complete 33-byte compressed serialization ''cbytes(Q)'' MUST be included in the intermediate hash input. It MUST NOT be replaced by ''xbytes(Q)''. The points ''Q'' and ''−Q'' have the same x-coordinate but are distinct group elements and represent distinct plain public keys at the parent aggregation node. Because ''pk_agg'' is required to be a valid canonical BIP327 plain public key and ''Q = cpoint(pk_agg)'', it holds that ''cbytes(Q) = pk_agg''. Writing ''cbytes(Q)'' in the algorithm makes explicit that the full point, including its parity, is committed to by the hash.

The message MUST NOT be included in ''NonceAggExt''. As specified in the paper,<ref name="paper" /> intermediate nonce binding factors are message-independent, allowing nested aggregation to be completed before the message is known. Only the root nonce binding factor commits to the message.

For the two-nonce instantiation, only the second nonce point is multiplied by ''b''. This follows from the paper's rule ''R<sub>j</sub> = b<sup>j−1</sup>⋅R'<sub>j</sub>''. Consequently: ''R<sub>1</sub> = R'<sub>1</sub>'', because ''b<sup>0</sup> = 1'', and ''R<sub>2</sub> = b⋅R'<sub>2</sub>'', because ''b<sup>1</sup> = b''.

As external nonces propagate toward the root, repeated applications of ''NonceAggExt'' cause a leaf signer's second nonce point to acquire the product of the intermediate binding factors on its path. The root binding factor is applied during signing, producing the accumulated factor ''b&#780; = b<sub>0</sub>⋅b<sub>1</sub>⋅...⋅b<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''.

====Points at Infinity====
''NonceAggExt'' MUST NOT replace a zero value of ''b'' with another value. It also MUST NOT replace a resulting point at infinity with ''G'' or any other point. If either component of the external nonce is the point at infinity, ''cbytes_ext'' encodes that component as 33 zero bytes. The parent node's unchanged BIP327 ''NonceAgg'' parses participant contributions using ''cpoint'', not ''cpoint_ext'', and therefore rejects such an external nonce and blames the nested participant that supplied it. For honestly generated nonces, this condition occurs only with negligible probability, including the negligible event ''b = 0''. A malicious participant or aggregator can deliberately cause an abort, but such a party can force the signing session to abort in any case. This intermediate behaviour is distinct from the BIP327 root behaviour. The root internal aggregate nonce ''out<sub>0</sub>'' is parsed using ''cpoint_ext'', and if the resulting final effective nonce would be the point at infinity, the BIP327 rule setting the final nonce to ''G'' applies unchanged.

===Session Context===

The '''session context''' of a leaf signer is a data structure consisting of:
* ''nonce_path'': the sequence ''(out<sub>0</sub>, ..., out<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)'' of 66-byte internal aggregate nonces at each level along the signer's path, ordered from the root toward the signer. Each element SHALL encode the concatenation of two compressed public keys (R<sub>1</sub> || R<sub>2</sub>) exactly as specified by BIP327 AggregateNonce.
* ''pk_tree'': the sequence ''(T<sub>0</sub>, ..., T<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)'' of cosigner-key multisets at each level along the signer's path, ordered from the root toward the signer. Each ''T<sub>d</sub>'' is a possibly empty multiset of 33-byte plain public keys. It excludes the participant occurrence by which the signer is represented at level ''d''. It MAY nevertheless contain one or more public keys bytewise equal to ''pk<sub>d</sub>'' if other participant occurrences at that level use the same plain public key, as duplicate public keys are permitted by BIP327.
* ''tweak<sub>1..v</sub>'': ''v'' 32-byte tweaks applied to the root aggregate key, with ''0 &le; v < 2<sup>32</sup>''.
* ''is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>'': ''v'' booleans, one tweak-mode flag for each element of ''tweak<sub>1..v</sub>''.
* ''m'': the message to sign, a byte array.

''nonce_path'' and ''pk_tree'' MUST have the same length ''&Lambda; &ge; 1''. Every resulting per-level key list ''L<sub>d</sub>'' MUST satisfy the input-size requirements of BIP327 ''KeySort'' and ''KeyAgg''. Unlike the BIP327 session context, the per-level key lists are determined jointly by the leaf signer's plain public key and ''pk_tree''. Consequently, different leaves of the same signer tree generally have different session contexts.

Although ''T<sub>d</sub>'' is treated cryptographically as a multiset, an implementation that supports contribution attribution MUST retain an unambiguous association between every key occurrence and the participant that supplied it. Sorting the public keys MUST NOT discard this association.

Any cached output derived from a session context, including the output of ''GetSessionValues'', SHALL be invalidated if any field of the session context changes.

The session context SHALL be treated as authenticated protocol state. Before producing a partial signature, a signer MUST verify that the root aggregate key, tweaks, message, per-level cosigner keys, and internal aggregate nonces correspond exactly to the signing session it intends to authorize.

===Signing===

The internal algorithm ''GetSessionValues'' derives the public per-session values for a leaf signer. It applies the recursive computations of NestedMuSig2 to the concrete key aggregation, tweaking, nonce handling, and BIP340 compatibility rules of BIP327.

The function ''GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx)'' returns the compressed 33-byte plain public key corresponding to the aggregate key contained in ''keyagg_ctx'' prior to the application of any subsequent tweaks.

Internal Algorithm ''GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)'':
* Inputs:
** ''session_ctx'': a session context as defined above.
** ''pk'': the leaf signer's 33-byte compressed plain public key.
* Let ''(nonce_path, pk_tree, tweak<sub>1..v</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>, m) = session_ctx''.
* Let ''&Lambda; = len(pk_tree)''.
* ''Fail'' if ''&Lambda; < 1'' or ''len(nonce_path) &ne; &Lambda;''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(tweak<sub>1..v</sub>) &ne; len(is_xonly_t<sub>1..v</sub>)''.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(pk) &ne; 33''.
* For ''d = 0, ..., &Lambda;−1'':
** If ''len(nonce_path[d]) &ne; 66'', fail with ''InvalidContribution'', blaming the level-''d'' nonce aggregator.
** Let ''R'<sub>1,d</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[d][0:33])''; if that fails, fail with ''InvalidContribution'', blaming the level-''d'' nonce aggregator.
** Let ''R'<sub>2,d</sub> = cpoint_ext(nonce_path[d][33:66])''; if that fails, fail with ''InvalidContribution'', blaming the level-''d'' nonce aggregator.
* Let ''pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> = pk''.
* Let ''L<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>} ∪ T<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)'', where ∪ denotes multiset union and inserts exactly one additional occurrence representing the signer, regardless of whether identical public keys already occur in T<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>.
* Let ''a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>, pk<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)''.
* Let ''keyagg_ctx = KeyAgg(L<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub>)''; fail if KeyAgg fails according to BIP327.
* For ''d = &Lambda;−2, ..., 0'':
** Let ''pk<sub>d</sub> = GetPlainPubkey(keyagg_ctx)''.
** Let ''b<sub>d+1</sub> = int(hash<sub>NestedMuSig/aggnoncecoef</sub>(nonce_path[d+1] || pk<sub>d</sub>)) mod n''.
** Let ''L<sub>d</sub> = KeySort({pk<sub>d</sub>} ∪ T<sub>d</sub>)'', where ∪ denotes multiset union and inserts exactly one occurrence representing the signer.
** Let ''a<sub>d</sub> = KeyAggCoeff(L<sub>d</sub>, pk<sub>d</sub>)''.
** Let ''keyagg_ctx = KeyAgg(L<sub>d</sub>)''; fail if KeyAgg fails according to BIP327.
* For ''i = 1, ..., v'':
** Let ''keyagg_ctx = ApplyTweak(keyagg_ctx, tweak<sub>i</sub>, is_xonly_t<sub>i</sub>)''; Fail if ApplyTweak fails according to BIP327.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, tacc) = keyagg_ctx''.
* Let ''b<sub>0</sub> = int(hash<sub>MuSig/noncecoef</sub>(nonce_path[0] || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n''.
* Let ''R' = R'<sub>1,0</sub> + b<sub>0</sub>⋅R'<sub>2,0</sub>''.
* If ''is_infinite(R')'', let the final nonce ''R = G''; otherwise, let ''R = R' ''.
* Let ''b&#780; = b<sub>0</sub>·b<sub>1</sub>·...·b<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''.
* Let ''c = int(hash<sub>BIP0340/challenge</sub>(xbytes(R) || xbytes(Q) || m)) mod n''.
* Let ''&#269; = c·a<sub>0</sub>·a<sub>1</sub>·...·a<sub>&Lambda;−1</sub> mod n''.
* Return ''(Q, gacc, tacc, b&#780;, R, c, &#269;)''.

For ''&Lambda; = 1'', no intermediate binding factor is computed. For a given sorted root key list, tweaks, aggregate nonce, and message, the values ''Q'', ''gacc'', ''tacc'', ''b<sub>0</sub>'', ''R'', and ''c'' are exactly the corresponding BIP327 session values. In this case, ''b&#780; = b<sub>0</sub>'' and ''&#269; = c·a<sub>0</sub>''.

The ordinary challenge ''c'' and the accumulated challenge coefficient ''&#269;'' are both returned. The distinction is necessary because leaf signing and partial-signature verification use ''&#269;'', while final root-level tweak aggregation uses the ordinary challenge ''c'', exactly as BIP327 uses its challenge when adding the ''tacc'' contribution.

The algorithm ''Sign(secnonce, sk, session_ctx)'' is identical to the BIP327 ''Sign'' algorithm except that the per-session values are obtained from ''GetSessionValues'' as specified in this document.

Algorithm ''Sign(secnonce, sk, session_ctx)'':
* Inputs:
** ''secnonce'': a 97-byte secret nonce, as returned by ''NonceGen'', that has never previously been used as input to ''Sign''.
** ''sk'': the signer's 32-byte secret key.
** ''session_ctx'': the signer's session context.
* ''Fail'' if ''len(secnonce) &ne; 97'' or ''len(sk) &ne; 32''.
* Let ''pk = IndividualPubkey(sk)''; fail if that fails.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, _, b&#780;, R, _, &#269;) = GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)''; fail if that fails.
* Let ''k'<sub>1</sub> = int(secnonce[0:32])''.
* Let ''k'<sub>2</sub> = int(secnonce[32:64])''.
* Let ''pk' = secnonce[64:97]'', interpreted as a compressed public key..
* The ''secnonce'' MUST NOT be used in any subsequent invocation of ''Sign'', regardless of whether this invocation succeeds or fails. Implementations SHOULD invalidate the secret nonce as soon as ''k'<sub>1</sub>'', ''k'<sub>2</sub>'', and ''pk' '' have been copied, for example by securely erasing its first 64 bytes or by using an API that consumes the secret-nonce object.
* ''Fail'' if ''k'<sub>i</sub> = 0'' or ''k'<sub>i</sub> &ge; n'' for ''i = 1, 2''.
* If ''has_even_y(R)'', let ''k<sub>i</sub> = k'<sub>i</sub>'' for ''i = 1, 2''; otherwise, let ''k<sub>i</sub> = n − k'<sub>i</sub>'' for ''i = 1, 2''.
* Let ''d' = int(sk)''; fail if ''d' = 0'' or ''d' &ge; n''.
* Let ''P = d'⋅G''.
* ''Fail'' if ''cbytes(P) &ne; pk' ''.
* Let ''g = 1'' if ''has_even_y(Q)''; otherwise, let ''g = −1 mod n''.
* Let ''d = g·gacc·d' mod n''.
* Let ''s = (k<sub>1</sub> + b&#780;·k<sub>2</sub> + &#269;·d) mod n''.
* Let ''psig = bytes(32, s)''.
* Let ''pubnonce = cbytes(k'<sub>1</sub>⋅G) || cbytes(k'<sub>2</sub>⋅G)''.
* If ''PartialSigVerifyInternal(psig, pubnonce, pk, session_ctx)'' returns failure, fail.
* Return the partial signature ''psig''.

As in BIP327, the signer's second-round output consists solely of ''psig''. The effective root aggregate nonce ''R'' is public and is recomputed from the session context by verifiers and by the root aggregator. 

The final self-verification step detects implementation errors and malformed internal state before a partial signature is released. Implementations SHOULD verify their own output by invoking ''PartialSigVerify'' prior to releasing a partial signature.

Implementations SHOULD run ''PartialSigVerify'' on their own output as a correctness self-check.

===Partial Signature Verification===

''PartialSigVerify'' verifies the second-round contribution of a signing participant. A participant is either an individual leaf signer or a nested aggregation node treated as a participant at its parent level. For an individual leaf signer, ''pubnonce'' is the 66-byte public nonce returned by ''NonceGen'', and ''session_ctx'' is the leaf signer's complete session context. For a nested aggregation node, ''pubnonce'' is the node's external nonce, ''pk'' is the node's plain aggregate public key, and ''session_ctx'' is the truncated session context covering the path from the root through the parent level at which that node participates. In that context, the final cosigner multiset excludes the participant occurrence represented by ''pk''.

Algorithm ''PartialSigVerify(psig, pubnonce, pk, session_ctx)'':
* Inputs:
** ''psig'': a 32-byte partial signature.
** ''pubnonce'': the participant's 66-byte public nonce. For a nested aggregation node, this is its external nonce.
** ''pk'': the participant's 33-byte plain public key.
** ''session_ctx'': the session context corresponding to the participant and its position in the signer tree.
* Return failure if ''len(psig) &ne; 32''.
* Return failure if ''len(pubnonce) &ne; 66''.
* Return failure if ''len(pk) &ne; 33''.
* Let ''(Q, gacc, _, b&#780;, R, _, &#269;) = GetSessionValues(session_ctx, pk)''; fail if that fails.
* Let ''s = int(psig)''; return failure if ''s &ge; n''.
* Let ''R<sub>*,1</sub> = cpoint(pubnonce[0:33])''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''R<sub>*,2</sub> = cpoint(pubnonce[33:66])''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''R&#780;' = R<sub>*,1</sub> + b&#780;⋅R<sub>*,2</sub>''.
* If ''has_even_y(R)'', let ''R&#780; = R&#780;' ''; otherwise, let ''R&#780; = −R&#780;' ''.
* Let ''P = cpoint(pk)''; return failure if that fails.
* Let ''g = 1'' if ''has_even_y(Q)''; otherwise, let ''g = −1 mod n''.
* Let ''g' = g·gacc mod n''.
* Return success if and only if ''s⋅G = R&#780; + (&#269;·g' mod n)⋅P''.

The verification equation follows directly from the signing equation. An honest participant computes ''s = k<sub>1</sub> + b&#780;·k<sub>2</sub> + &#269;·g·gacc·d' mod n'', and therefore ''s⋅G = R&#780; + &#269;·g·gacc·P''.

If every required contribution verifies against session contexts derived from the same signer tree, root aggregate key, tweak sequence, root aggregate nonce, and message, and every aggregator performs the specified modular aggregation, the final signature produced by ''PartialSigAgg'' passes BIP340 verification. Verification of contributions against mutually inconsistent session contexts does not provide this guarantee.

As with BIP327, partial signatures are '''not''' proofs of knowledge or possession. A malicious party controlling more than one participant position can construct a partial signature that verifies for a public key whose secret key it does not know, but it will then be unable to produce a valid contribution for at least one of its other participant positions.<ref>''Forgery with a fake key in MuSig2'', https://gist.github.com/AdamISZ/ca974ed67889cedc738c4a1f65ff620b</ref> Consequently, successful partial-signature verification MUST NOT be interpreted as proof that the purported signer knows the corresponding secret key.

The protocol purpose of partial-signature verification is to identify disruptive participants. The internal invocation performed by ''Sign'' additionally serves as an implementation correctness check, detecting local computation errors before the partial signature is released.